<!-- table:stage-gate-1.criteria role=labels key=Criterion -->

## Criteria

Evidence must cite **rows or facts**, not just a filename.

| Criterion | Status | Evidence | To close | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Operating map + exception inventory at standard — all nine elements, exceptions with frequency and rule holder | | | | |
| Stakeholder map — **five roles identified correctly**, decision rights defensible | | | | |
| Readiness scorecard — **the data landmines found** | | | | |
| Draft ontology — **canonical grain chosen and defended**; grain mismatches identified as the cause of what breaks weekly | | | | |
| Evidence-handling terms signed; monitoring constraint checked | | | | |

<!-- table:stage-gate-1.behaviours role=labels key=Behaviour -->

## Behaviours

Artefacts alone do not pass this gate.

| Behaviour | Observed | Where |
|---|---|---|
| Chose **observation over interview**, unprompted, at least once | | |
| **Treated resistance as information** — went and watched instead of persuading | | |
| **Correctly identified at least one thing that should not be built** | | |
| Can state the sponsor's real problem **in one sentence that is not what they asked for** | | |

The last one is the sharpest test in the gate. If the team can only restate the request, discovery has not happened yet.

<!-- table:stage-gate-1.anti-patterns role=labels key=Check -->

## Anti-pattern check

| Check | Confirmed |
|---|---|
| Not all green on first pass — on a real engagement that means it was written from intent, not evidence | |
| "Partial" used only with a stated remainder and an owner | |
| Readiness scorecard checked twice: possible ≠ agreed ≠ **provisioned** | |
| Evidence cites rows, not filenames | |

